'''Garbage masher 3263827''',<ref name="SWCL">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> also known as '''trash compactor 32-6-3827''', was a [[garbage compactor]]<ref name="Complete Vehicles 2018">[[Star Wars: Complete Vehicles (2018)|''Star Wars: Complete Vehicles'' (2018)]]</ref> for recyclable waste<ref name="SWCL" /> aboard the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|DS-1 platform]], better known as the Death Star.

==History==
{{Quote|One thing's for sure. We're all gonna be a lot thinner!|Han Solo|<ref name="ANH" />}}
[[File:NowhereToRun-Awakenings.png|thumb|left|200px|Leia, Han, Chewbacca, and Luke being watched by the dianoga]]
In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas: Updated Edition]]''</ref> upon [[Rescue of Princess Leia|freeing]] [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] from the first [[Death Star]]'s [[Detention Level]], [[Han Solo]], [[Chewbacca]], and [[Luke Skywalker]] were temporarily stranded inside garbage masher 3263827, along with the princess. Owing to their [[armor]] and weapons, garbage chute [[sensor]]s believed that they were recyclable waste.<ref name="SWCL" /> [[Omi]], a [[Force-sensitive]] [[Diet|carnivorous]] [[dianoga]], proceeded to baptize Skywalker in accordance to her people's tradition.<ref name="The Baptist">{{StoryCite|story=The Baptist|book=From a Certain Point of View}}</ref> Luke and his companions would nearly [[Death|die]] when the masher's walls started to close in order to compress the waste it contained. However, Skywalker's [[droid]]s [[C-3PO]] and [[R2-D2]], who had remained behind in safety, managed to disable all garbage compactors on the Detention Level of the Death Star, thus saving the rescue team from a gruesome death.<ref name="ANH" />

